/// `GenServerIdleTimeout`, adapted: Beamtalk has no GenServer idle
/// timeout, so it sends itself the bare `#timeout` and `#read_timeout`
/// messages that once meant one. Neither may be taken for the read timer.
RecordingHandler subclass: StrayTimeoutHandler

  handleConnection: _sock :: Socket state: st :: Object -> HandlerResult =>
    self pid send: #timeout
    self pid send: #read_timeout
    HandlerResult continue: st
